.TH HAMSTIK 1 "HAMSTIK WORK CREATE"
.SH NAME
hamstik work create \- Create a work item
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hamstik work create [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a work item
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --title
Work item title
.TP
.B --description
Description text
.TP
.B --description-file
Description source (path, or - for stdin)
.TP
.B --description-editor
Author the description in $VISUAL/$EDITOR instead of passing text
Choices: true, false
.TP
.B --type
Work item type
Choices: task, bug, story, feature, epic
.TP
.B --status
Initial status
Choices: backlog, todo, in_progress, in_review, done
.TP
.B --priority
Priority
Choices: low, medium, high, urgent
.TP
.B --assignee
Assignee user id (or `me`)
.TP
.B --sprint
Sprint id
.TP
.B --parent
Parent work item key (or parent UUID)
.TP
.B --story-points
Story point estimate
.TP
.B --due-date
Due date (RFC 3339)
.TP
.B --idempotency-key
Explicit idempotency key
